# Set this for EVERY environment — Production, Preview and Development.
# Missing, createClient() is handed undefined and throws while the module
# is still loading, so React never mounts: the page paints the background
# colour from CSS and stops. It does not look like a missing variable, it
# looks like a dead site, and it will do that on a build whose deploy log
# is green. This has now cost two evenings, once on the key below and
# once here, so check the ticks per environment rather than the value.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
# Despite the name, this now holds a PUBLISHABLE key — sb_publishable_…,
# from Project Settings → API Keys. The legacy eyJ… anon key it used to
# hold is switched off at the project, so a build carrying one gets 401
# from the gateway on every request including sign-in. The name is kept
# because renaming it means a window where the deployed build reads a
# variable the host no longer has.
#
# Vite inlines this at BUILD time. Setting it on the host does nothing
# until the next deploy — and check it PER ENVIRONMENT: a value saved to
# Development only will leave Production serving whatever it had, which
# looks exactly like a working change until the old key is revoked.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
# The domain this build is served from, no trailing slash. Substituted
# into index.html's canonical link, og:url and the two image URLs, which
# have to be absolute for a link preview to resolve. Unset, it falls back
# to https://cabbys.aw — so set this the day the real domain is bought.
VITE_SITE_URL=
# One Google Maps Platform key, shared by everything map-related: live
# address search in the booking card and picker, the interactive route map,
# its static-image fallback, and the driving line drawn on both. Falls back
# to "type it, pick your area" and a drawn sketch of the island when unset.
# On the Google Cloud project this key belongs to, enable "Places API
# (New)", "Maps JavaScript API", "Maps Static API" and "Routes API", turn
# on billing, and restrict the key by HTTP referrer to this site's own
# domain(s) — never ship an unrestricted key.
# Vite inlines this at BUILD time, so setting it on the host after the fact
# does nothing until the next deploy.
VITE_GOOGLE_PLACES_KEY=
# The WhatsApp account guests and drivers reach you on. Digits only, FULL
# international form: country code, no +, no 00, and no leading national
# zero. A Dutch mobile is 316…, not 06…; an Aruban one is 297…. Anything
# else resolves to wa.me/<nonsense>, which opens WhatsApp's own landing
# page rather than a conversation — a link that looks alive and goes
# nowhere, which is the hardest kind of broken to notice.
#
# Unset is a supported state, not a fault: every chat link in the app
# hides itself and the copy stops naming a channel it cannot offer. Admin
# → Settings reports which of the two you are in, and is the fastest way
# to check.
#
# Vite inlines this at BUILD time like the rest. Editing the value in the
# host's dashboard changes nothing until the next build, and a redeploy
# that reuses the build cache can hand back the very bundle you are
# trying to replace — so untick it when the value is what changed.
VITE_WHATSAPP_NUMBER=
# Optional — payment goes live only when these are set
VITE_STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=
